  <page_number>57</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">
      <i>Illúmque armatis urbibus expulit,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="2">
      <i>Minata cædes vinclàque turpia,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Durisq;, cedentem procellis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Signa sequi Lotharena iussit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Sed magna Regis mens violentiam,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Sævósque fortis contudit impetus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Virésque prouisis minores</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Consiliis melior subegit.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Sic sic minantes exitium Iouí</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Pallas Gigantes Ægide perdidit:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Quum fulminantem iuuit illa</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Consilio potiore patrem.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Non vis furenti profuit impia</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Turbæ, nec Offæ Pelion insitus.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Vis sola conatúsque semper</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Mole ruunt propria nefasti.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Nunc fraudulentis hostibus obrutis,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Rex magne, motus discute turbidos:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Pacémque languenti benignus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Perpetuam patriæ redona.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Nam tota cunctis urbibus ingemit</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Oppressa diris Gallia cladibus,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Tristésque mactatis cruenta</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Ciuibus ingeminat querelas.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Franciscus ex quo mollia turpiter</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Euertit audax otia Guisius,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="27">
      <i>Belliqué ciuilis scelestus</i>
    </l>
    <l n="28">
      <i>Francigenas violauit author.</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse is printed with indented lines in one run; I have kept the line breaks within one paragraph. Doubtful readings: "Illúmque" accent as printed; "Iouí" (final letter could be Iouis) [?] not marked in text because the form is clear enough; "Turbæ" is printed with a ligature-like sign, read as æ; "Durisq;" q with a sign; "mactatis" printed with a ligature-like form, read as mactatis. Long s normalised to s; u/v and i/j normalised. Greek or Hebrew: none.</notes>
</page>
